{
  "query": "desktop no network connection wired ethernet",
  "reason": "Find article for desktop network outage"
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: James O'Connor (Operations, Warehouse Supervisor, user_id 8, hours 06:00-14:00 CT) says his desktop BL-DT-0108 has no network, and the floor 2 printer BL-PR-FL2 is down. Checked: account is active and not locked or blocked. BL-DT-0108 (Windows 11, wired desktop) shows offline, last check-in 2026-10-11 00:57 UTC, no warnings, disk is fine. BL-PR-FL2 shows offline, last check-in 2026-10-10 21:57 UTC, no warnings or error codes. Finding: two devices are offline, both with no warnings and with last check-ins 3 hours apart. That could point to a shared switch, port or floor 2 network fault rather than two separate device faults, but I don't know if the desktop is on floor 2. No KB covers a wired desktop with no network, and KB-014 says to escalate if the office network is down for several people. I've asked the user to check the desktop's network cable and link light, restart the desktop, find out whether colleagues nearby are affected, and have someone check the printer screen and power cycle it (KB-022). Still needed: check switch and port status for floor 2 and the desktop's port, confirm how widespread it is, and send someone onsite if the printer stays offline after a power cycle with no error (KB-022 escalate condition).",
  "reason": "Two devices offline, possibly a shared network fault. No KB covers a wired desktop with no network, and the printer has no error showing."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry about the rough morning. I checked, and both your desktop and the floor 2 printer show as disconnected from our network. Since both dropped off around the same time, it could be one network problem behind both, so I've passed this to our Tier 2 network team. A few things you can try while you wait: 1) Make sure the network cable is firmly plugged into the back of your desktop and the wall socket, and check whether the small light next to the cable's socket on the desktop is lit. Then restart the desktop. 2) Ask the people near you whether their computers are online. That tells us if more people are affected. 3) If someone is near the printer, have them check its screen for errors like a paper jam, no toner or an open door. Then turn it off, wait 30 seconds and turn it back on. Please reply with what you find, especially if other people are affected too. Tier 2 will follow up with you.",
  "internal_note": "User 8, account active and not locked. BL-DT-0108 is offline (last check-in 2026-10-11 00:57 UTC), no warnings. BL-PR-FL2 is offline (last check-in 2026-10-10 21:57 UTC), no warnings. The two outages may be linked (shared switch, port or floor network). No KB covers a wired desktop with no network. Followed the KB-022 quick checks and gave the user the power-cycle steps and the KB-014-style checks. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) to check switch and port status and how widespread this is. Didn't suggest KB-024 (another printer) because the desktop is offline too, so it can't print anywhere right now.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-022",
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
